**Theorem 9.1 (an attained native fiber with charged acquisition).**
Fix any three states $Q\subset P$ in Proposition 7.1. For every
$H\ge0$, put $n=2^H$ and $D=9+H$. There is a correct preparation
and reader on every original $t\in\mathcal F_D$ with complete
attained alphabet exactly

$$
|S_D|-3^n+1.
\tag{RCE.33}
$$

It merges precisely the canonical trees in $T_H(Q^n)$ into one
name and names all other canonical trees separately. Sufficient
resources on every source are

$$
T_{\mathrm{prep}}=2^D-1,\qquad
Q_{\mathrm{prep}}\le D,\qquad
A_{\mathrm{prep}}=(D-1)2^D+1.
\tag{RCE.34}
$$

The optional one late Read has length at most $D$ and is selected
before any authentic count. At $H=0$ these bounds are $511$
preparation Reads and $4097$ submitted letters, with
$|S_9|-2$ attained names.

Proof. Before any target, submit all actual words $Rq$, $q\in W_D$,
including absent replies. They determine $\pi_D(v)$ by the credited
FMR scan. Compute the described finite membership name and export
only that fixed-width name. The public scan, allocation and a
padded finite computation schedule can depend on $D$ alone. All
other acquired descriptions, control distinctions, buffers and
timing records are isolated under the paid service of Definition
1.1. Thus every accessible surviving distinction is a function of
the name and public inputs.

The $3^n$ special trees are distinct actual members of $S_D$;
every other canonical tree has its own distinct name. All names
are attained by canonical actual sources, giving (RCE.33).
Counting the scan gives $\sum_{l=0}^{D-1}2^l=2^D-1$ calls and
$\sum_{l=0}^{D-1}(l+1)2^l=(D-1)2^D+1$ letters. This is a
deterministic effective preparation for every variable shape, not
a preassigned unacquired coloring.

After a singleton name, the installed table determines all its
canonical target factors and no Read is needed. For the special
name, targets strictly above the outer frontier are branch.
Every other request first enters one actual $Q$ block and either
ends above that block's inner height-six frontier, again branch,
or enters a core module. Its possible module states form a subset
of at most three core states, determined by $Q$ and its public
module address. Select the $L$ or $RL$ query of Lemma 6.2 and
prefix it by $R$, the outer height-$H$ address and the inner
height-six address. Its length is at most
$1+H+6+2=D$. Its reply determines the requested module factor;
no hash row or full block identity is supplied to the reader.

Every queried occurrence is actually present on the canonical
special fiber, and its literal lies in the acquired boundary.
On every original source with that name, canonicalization
preserves the queried reply and the requested factor. The credited
all-count law (RCE.5) therefore gives (RCE.2) for every later
authentic count, including initially absent targets. No preparation
transcript is accessed and no second observation is made.

Source-independent table generation, canonical-state membership
computation, control and workspace, predictor size, authentication,
isolation and physical time remain separate paid resources. These
codes are deliberately nonoptimal; (RCE.33) is not a claim about
the exact optimum. $\square$

